    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe logic is placed well \u2014 `toLocality(owner)` mirrors the existing `toMembershipTier(owner)` helper exactly (same `@Mapping` expression style, same default-method-on-interface pattern, constant declared right above its consumer), so the derivation lives in the right unit and nothing is duplicated or turned into a catch-all. One idiomatic issue:\n\n- **Fully-qualified names instead of imports (`OwnerMapper.java:45`).** The file already establishes the convention of importing `java.util` types at the top (`import java.util.Collection;`, `import java.util.List;`). The new code instead writes `java.util.Map<String, String>` and `java.util.Map.of(...)` inline. A maintainer following this file's own style would add `import java.util.Map;` and use the bare `Map` / `Map.of(...)`, matching the surrounding declarations. Minor, but it's a visible deviation from the file's established idiom.",
